[center][size=6][color=#42FA60][b]FO4 Community Shaders[/b][/color][/size]
[b]Modern rendering for Fallout 4.[/b]
[color=#A8B5A8]Configured through Dear Modding UI[/color][/center]

[b]FO4 Community Shaders[/b] brings modern lighting, shadows, reflections, weather effects, and upscaling to Fallout 4 as a single F4SE plugin. It is a port of [url=https://github.com/community-shaders/skyrim-community-shaders]Skyrim Community Shaders[/url], rebuilt on the game's own renderer.

Every feature ships turned off. Enable only what you want, and the rest of the game renders exactly as before.

[color=#FFB84D][b]Beta:[/b] Features are still being developed and tested. Expect rough edges, and please report what you find.[/color]

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]FEATURES[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Screen Space Shadows:[/b] Contact shadows and finer shadow detail.[/*]
[*][b]Terrain Shadows:[/b] Long-range shadows cast by distant terrain.[/*]
[*][b]Screen Space GI:[/b] Ambient occlusion and indirect lighting.[/*]
[*][b]Inverse Square Lighting:[/b] More natural light falloff.[/*]
[*][b]Exponential Height Fog:[/b] Weather-driven fog that thins with altitude.[/*]
[*][b]Dynamic Cubemaps:[/b] Reflections that respond to the surrounding scene.[/*]
[*][b]Wetness Effects:[/b] Rain-darkened surfaces and wet reflections.[/*]
[*][b]Water Effects:[/b] Sunlight caustics on submerged surfaces.[/*]
[*][b]Upscaling:[/b] TAA, FSR 3/4, and DLSS.[/*]
[*][b]Frame Generation:[/b] FSR 3/4 and DLSS, including supported Multi Frame Generation modes.[/*]
[*][b]Motion Vector Fixes:[/b] Motion-data corrections for temporal rendering.[/*]
[*][b]Performance Overlay:[/b] FPS, frame-time, and latency graphs.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout 4 [b]1.11.240[/b] on Windows (OG and NG at your own risk)[/*]
[*][url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url] matching your game version[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/47327]Address Library for F4SE Plugins[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/Dear-Modding-FO4/DearModdingUI]Dear Modding UI[/url] for the in-game menu (recommended)[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/84214]Addictol[/url] for engine stability and bug fixes (recommended)[/*]
[/list]

Upscaling and frame generation need a DX12-capable GPU. DLSS requires an NVIDIA RTX card, and FSR 4 requires a compatible AMD Radeon card.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]INSTALLATION & USAGE[/b][/color][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install F4SE, Address Library, and Dear Modding UI.[/*]
[*]Install FO4 Community Shaders through your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Launch Fallout 4 through F4SE and open Community Shaders in Dear Modding UI.[/*]
[*]Enable the features you want, then restart the game.[/*]
[/list]

Enabling or disabling a feature takes effect after a restart. Settings for enabled features apply live.

Without Dear Modding UI, enable features in [b]Data\F4SE\Plugins\FO4CommunityShaders\FO4CommunityShaders.User.toml[/b]:
[code][features.ScreenSpaceShadows]
load = true[/code]

[b]Hotkeys:[/b] [b]F10[/b] toggles the performance overlay, and [b]Ctrl+F12[/b] writes a diagnostic dump. Rebind them in Dear Modding UI.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]FAQ[/b][/color][/size]
[b]Is this mod compatible with ENB?[/b]
I will now have to publicly execute you.

[b]What about HDR?[/b]
Windows Auto HDR and NVIDIA RTX HDR work. Native HDR output mods such as RenoDX or Special K HDR are not supported.

[b]I installed it and nothing changed.[/b]
Every feature ships turned off. Enable the ones you want in Dear Modding UI, then restart the game.

[b]Does it work on the OG or NG runtime?[/b]
The code paths exist, and they have received exactly zero testing. Have fun. Only 1.11.240 is supported.

[b]Which upscaler should I use?[/b]
DLSS on NVIDIA RTX cards and FSR 4 on compatible AMD Radeon cards. TAA and FSR 3 work on other DX12-capable GPUs.

[b]Frame generation won't turn on.[/b]
Switch the game to borderless windowed mode.

[b]Terrain Shadows does nothing.[/b]
It needs a terrain heightmap exported with xLODGen.

[b]Why is the first launch slow?[/b]
Shaders compile after installing or updating. Later launches load them from the cache.

[b]The game froze for a moment when I changed upscalers.[/b]
That's expected. Switching upscaling or frame-generation methods briefly pauses rendering.

[b]Can I add or remove it mid-playthrough?[/b]
Yes. It has no plugin file and writes nothing to your saves.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]LINKS & SUPPORT[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-community-shaders][b]GitHub Repository[/b][/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-community-shaders/issues/new/choose][b]Report an Issue[/b][/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-community-shaders/releases][b]Development Builds[/b][/url][/*]
[/list]

When reporting a problem, include your mod version, GPU, the features you enabled, and [b]FO4CommunityShaders.log[/b]. Attach [b]FO4CommunityShaders.User.toml[/b] if you edited it.

Logs are saved in: [b]Documents\My Games\Fallout4\F4SE\[/b]

